  "markdown": "<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">\n\n<description>A technical cross-section diagram showing the construction detail of a curb installation. The diagram illustrates a concrete curb unit labeled 'NYSDOT TYPE (NVF)' resting on a 'DRY MIX CONCRETE CONTINUOUS BED' which sits on 'COMPACTED SUBGRADE'. To the right of the curb is 'CONCRETE BACKING 3500 PSI' with dimensions of 8\" in height. The overall height from the bottom of the dry mix bed to the top of the curb is 16\" (8\" backing + 4\" bed + 4\" unspecified bottom section, though the graphic shows 8\" backing + 4\" bed, totaling 12\" plus the curb height). The curb width is 5\". A note 'SEE NOTE 1' points to the space left of the curb, where pavement meets the curb. There is a 'FACE OF CURB' vertical reference line.</description> The diagram includes the following text labels: 'FACE OF CURB', '5\"', 'FINISHED GRADE', 'SEE NOTE 1', 'NYSDOT TYPE (NVF)', '16\"', '8\"', '4\"', 'PLACE CONCRETE BACKING TO BOTTOM OF BASE COURSE', 'CONCRETE BACKING 3500 PSI', '6\" TYP', 'DRY MIX CONCRETE CONTINUOUS BED', 'COMPACTED SUBGRADE'.</figure>\n\nNOTES:\n 1. FOR NEW CONSTRUCTION, A 6\" CURB REVEAL SHALL\nBE MAINTAINED. MATCH EXISTING REVEAL FOR CURB\nREPLACEMENT OR RESETTING.\n\n\nNO SCALE\n\n\n[⚜]\nALBANY\nNEW YORK | EST. 1686\n[⚜]\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E. City Engineer\n\n\n<table>\n<tr><td>CITY OF ALBANY - DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL NAME: GRANITE CURB INSTALLATION DETAIL</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<table>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No.<br>C-1</td><td>FILE NAME:<br>C-1.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED<br>05/01/02</td><td>REVISION DATE<br>03/26/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">\n\n<description>This is a technical construction cross-section diagram showing the detail of a wedge curb installation. The diagram depicts layers of road construction from bottom to top: a thick Subbase Course at the bottom, an Asphalt Base Course layer above it, and an Asphalt Concrete Top Course forming the upper layer. A wedge-shaped curb section, labeled '2'-0\" WEDGE CURB', is integrated into the top course, sloping upwards towards a 'FINISHED GRADE (TYP)' line. The finished grade is indicated with a hatched texture and sits 4\" above the edge of the asphalt. There is a 12\" dimension marked at the outer edge. The diagram includes specific annotations: '1-1/2\" TOP COURSE' pointing to the thickness of the top asphalt layer, and 'TACK COAT (TYP)' indicating the interface between asphalt layers.</description></figure>\n\nNOTES:\n 1. MAINTAIN EXISTING TRAVEL LANE(S)\nWIDTH PER TRAFFIC ENGINEERING.\n\n\nNO SCALE\n\n\n[⚜]\nALBANY\nNEW YORK | EST. 1686\n[⚜]\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer\n\n\n<table>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY – DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br><br>ASPHALT WEDGE CURB<br>DETAIL</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No.<br>C-2</td><td>FILE NAME:<br>C-2.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED<br>05/01/02</td><td>REVISION DATE<br>03/26/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">\n\n<description>This diagram illustrates a technical plan view of an ADA-compliant curb ramp. The ramp features a central section with an ADA detectable warning surface (represented by a grid of circles) and two flanking sections. Each section is labeled with a slope indicator of '1:12'. The overall width is divided into three 5'-0\" segments along the curb line. The surface texture is indicated as 'BROOM FINISH (TYP)'. Annotations provide guidance: 'ADA DETECTABLE WARNING' and 'REFER TO CR-2 AND NYSDOT 608-01 STANDARD SHEETS FOR PLACEMENT AND CONFIGURATION'. The drawing clearly delineates the curb boundary.</description></figure>\n\nNOTE:\n1. CURB SHALL BE FLUSH WITH\nPAVEMENT AT ROADWAY.\n2. SEE STANDARD DETAILS FOR CURB\nAND SIDEWALK INSTALLATION.\n3. SEE STANDARD DETAIL FOR ADA\nDETECTABLE WARNING STRIP INSTALLATION.\n4. INSTALLATION SHALL MEET ALL\nAPPLICABLE ADA CODES AND STANDARDS.\n5. REFER TO NYSDOT 608-01 STANDARD\nSHEETS FOR APPLICABLE CURB RAMP LAYOUT\nFOR EACH INDIVIDUAL CURB RAMP\n\n\n[FLEUR-DE-LIS SYMBOL]\nALBANY\nNEW YORK | EST. 1686\n[FLEUR-DE-LIS SYMBOL]\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer\n\n\n<table>\n<tr><td>CITY OF ALBANY - DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL NAME: ADA CURB RAMP DETAIL</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<table>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No. CR-1</td><td>FILE NAME: CR-1.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED 05/01/02</td><td>REVISION DATE 03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\nNO SCALE\n\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">\n\n<description>This is a technical plan view diagram of a ramp section, illustrating surface finish requirements and dimensions. The diagram is rectangular, oriented vertically, and features two distinct zones.</description>\n\n1. Top Section:\n- Contains horizontal line hatching, labeled: \"REMAINING PORTION OF RAMP TO RECEIVE BROOM FINISH IN ACCORDANCE WITH ADA STANDARDS\".\n\n2. Bottom Section:\n- Contains a pattern of circles (dots) representing a detectable warning surface, labeled: \"CAST IN PLACE DETECTABLE WARNING SURFACE TILE BY ARMOR TILE OR APPROVED EQUAL\".\n\n3. Annotations and Dimensions:\n- A dimension arrow spans the width of the bottom section, labeled: \"WARNING STRIP SHALL EXTEND OVER FULL WIDTH OF RAMP (5'-0\" MIN)\".\n- A dimension arrow on the right side indicates the depth of the warning strip: \"2'-0\" MIN\".\n- Two arrows labeled \"A\" pointing towards each other indicate a section cut line.\n- Text label at the bottom: \"PLAN\".</figure>\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">PLAN\n\n\n\n<description>This is a construction detail diagram showing a cross-section of a sidewalk or ramp feature. At the top center, there is a 'CAST IN PLACE DETECTABLE WARNING TILE' labeled 'NYSDOT ITEM 608.21', which sits flush with the adjacent concrete sections on either side. Below this tile is a layer of '4\" CONCRETE'. Underneath the concrete layer, spanning the width of the concrete, is a base layer labeled '6\" MIN. CRUSHED STONE'. The diagram illustrates the installation profile of the detectable warning surface.</description></figure>\n\nNOTES:\n 1. THE COLOR OF THE DETECTABLE WARNING SURFACE\nSHALL BE DARK GRAY, MUNSELL BOOK NOTATION\nBG-PB 3/5. THIS COLOR IS THE CITY OF ALBANY\nSTANDARD COLOR FOR DETECTABLE WARNING\nSURFACES.\n 2. SEE STANDARD DETAILS FOR CURB, SIDEWALK,\nAND SIDEWALK RAMP INSTALLATION.\n 3. INSTALLATION SHALL MEET ALL APPLICABLE\nADA CODES AND STANDARDS.\n\n\nNO SCALE\n\n\n⚜️\nALBANY\nNEW YORK | EST. 1686\n⚜️\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer\n\n\n<table>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY - DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br>ADA DETECTABLE WARNING<br>STRIP DETAIL</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No. CR-2</td><td>FILE NAME: CR-2.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED 09/16/03</td><td>REVISION DATE 03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\nSECTION A-A\n\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">\n\n<description>The figure is a technical diagram illustrating the construction detail of a driveway apron intersecting with a concrete sidewalk. The perspective is an isometric view showing the transition between a paved roadway, a driveway, and a sidewalk.</description> Key labels and annotations in the diagram include: \n- \"6\" CONCRETE (SEE DETAIL SW-1)\" pointing to the concrete surface.\n- \"NEW OR EXISTING DRIVEWAY\" indicating the driveway area.\n- \"MAX. GRADIENT 1:12 (AND 1:50 CROSS-SLOPE IF WITHIN WALKING PATH)\" with a directional arrow indicating the slope.\n- \"BROOM FINISH (TYP)\" with arrows pointing to the textured concrete surfaces.\n- \"MATCH EXISTING GRADE (TYP)\" with an arrow pointing to the transition edge.\n- \"CONCRETE SIDEWALK\" labeling the sidewalk section.\n- \"GRANITE CURBING\" pointing to the curb element.\n- \"MATCH EXISTING\" labeling the edge of the sidewalk.\n- \"6'-0\"\" dimension labels indicating the width of the driveway ramp transition.\n- \"VARIES, MATCH EXISTING DRIVEWAY WIDTH\" indicating the width parameter.\n- \"PAVED ROADWAY\" at the bottom of the diagram.</figure>\n\nNOTE:\n1. CURB REVEALS SHALL BE 1/2” MAX WHERE\nRAMP MEETS PAVEMENT AT ROADWAY.\n2. SIDEWALK SHALL BE INSTALLED FLUSH WITH\nEXISTING DRIVEWAY.\n3. SEE STANDARD SIDEWALK DETAIL FOR\nSIDEWALK INSTALLATION.\nNO SCALE\n\n\n[FLORAL_ORNAMENT]\nALBANY\nNEW YORK | EST. 1686\n[FLORAL_ORNAMENT]\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer\n\n\n<table>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY – DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br>DRIVEWAY/SIDEWALK DROP CURB</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No.<br>DW-1</td><td>FILE NAME:<br>DW-1.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED<br>05/01/02</td><td>REVISION DATE<br>03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">\n\n<description>This diagram depicts a cross-sectional view of a pavement repair detail, specifically showing the layers involved in a trench restoration. At the top surface, there is an existing asphalt pavement on either side, with a 18-inch section marked as the 'Limits of Disturbance' on both sides of the center cut. The repair structure consists of, from top to bottom: a 2-inch thick asphalt pavement top course (specified for 9.5mm or 6.5mm aggregate), an 8-inch concrete foundation for the pavement, and a 12-inch subbase course. Below the subbase is the trench backfill, which is noted to be filled in 6-inch lifts and compacted per specifications. The sides of the excavation are marked as 'Excavation Limits', and a 'Tack Coat' is applied at the interface between the new asphalt and existing pavement. The cuts in the existing pavement are labeled as 'Sawcut Pavement (Typ)'.</description></figure>\n\nNOTE:\n 1. IF LIMITS OF TRENCHING EXCEEDS 50 FEET,\nCONTRACTOR SHALL COMPLETE CURB TO CURB\nMILLING PER CITY DETAIL SR-3; UNLESS OTHERWISE\nORDERED BY CITY OF ALBANY DEPARTMENT OF GENERAL SERVICES.\n 2. ALL PAVEMENT MARKINGS DISTURBED SHALL BE\nRESTORED TO THE SATISFACTION OF THE CITY\nOF ALBANY DIVISION OF TRAFFIC ENGINEERING.\n 3. ALL JOINTS TO BE SEALED WITH ASPHALT\nEMULSION (AC-20)\n 4. ASHPHALT, CONCRETE TACK COAT, TRENCH BACKFILL AND OTHER\nMATERIALS AND OPERATIONS SHALL CONFORM TO NYSDOT STANDARDS AND\nSPECIFICATIONS UNLESS NOTED OR DIRECTED OTHERWISE BY THE CITY.\nNO SCALE\n\n\n<table>\n<tr><td rowspan=\"3\">⚜️<br>ALBANY<br>NEW YORK | EST. 1686<br>⚜️<br><br>Katherine M. Sheehan, Mayor<br>Howard M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer</td><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY – DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br>STREET RESTORATION<br>DETAIL</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No. SR-1</td><td>FILE NAME: SR-1.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED 05/01/02</td><td>REVISION DATE 03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">\n\n<description>This technical cross-section diagram illustrates the construction detail for a trench backfill and pavement restoration. The diagram displays a cut-away view of the ground layers. At the top, there is a section of existing asphalt pavement with '18\"' extensions on either side indicating the 'LIMITS OF DISTURBANCE'. The center of the pavement section is labeled '10\" TEMPORARY 2500 PSI CONCRETE', with a note instructing to 'MILL CONCRETE AND REPLACE WITH 2\" ASPHALT TOP COURSE AFTER WINTER TIME PERIOD'. Below the concrete layer, there is a '12\" SUBBASE COURSE COMPACT IN 6\" LIFTS'. A dashed line outlines the 'EXCAVATION LIMITS' extending downward, containing the 'TRENCH BACKFILL, BACKFILL IN 6\" LIFTS, COMPACT PER SPECIFICATIONS'. Annotations point to specific features: 'EXISTING ASPHALT PAVEMENT (TYP)', 'SEAL ALL JOINTS', and 'SAWCUT PAVEMENT (TYP)'.</description></figure>\n\nNOTES:\n1. CONTRACTOR SHALL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR MAINTAINING TEMPORARY WEARING SURFACE\n2 UNTIL PERMANENT PAVEMENT IS IN PLACE. TEMPORARY CONCRETE WEARING SURFACE\n3 SHALL BE REMOVED AND PERMANENT PAVEMENT RESTORATION COMPLETED NO LATER\n4 THAN MAY 15. PERMANENT PAVEMENT RESTORATION SHALL BE INSTALLED IN ACCORDANCE\n5 WITH CITY STANDARD DETAILS AND TO THE SATISFACTION OF THE CITY OF ALBANY.\n2. ALL JOINTS TO BE SEALED WITH ASPHALT EMULSION (AC-20)\n3. ALL WORK SHALL BE INSPECTED AND APPROVED BY THE CITY.\nNO SCALE\n\n\n⚜⚜⚜\nALBANY\nNEW YORK | EST. 1686\n⚜⚜⚜\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer\n\n\n<table>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY – DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br>STREET RESTORATION - WINTER CONDITIONS<br>NOVEMBER 1 - APRIL 15</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No.<br>SR-2</td><td>FILE NAME:<br>SR-2.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED<br>05/01/02</td><td>REVISION DATE<br>03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">\n\n<description>This diagram illustrates a cross-section of a roadway undergoing trench excavation and pavement milling. The top section shows the 'LIMITS OF ROADWAY' with a sloped asphalt surface. A highlighted layer indicates a '2\" ASPHALT CONCRETE TOP COURSE' applied over a 'TACK COAT'. A dashed outline in the center indicates the 'LIMITS OF TRENCH EXCAVATION', with a note instructing to 'REFER TO DETAIL SR-1 FOR FULL DEPTH PAVING RESTORATION REQUIREMENTS'. An arrow points to the top pavement layer with the instruction: 'MILL A MINIMUM OF 2\" OF EXISTING TOP COURSE FROM ROADWAY'. Below the diagram, there are two notes: '1. PAVEMENT MILLING OPERATION SHALL EXTEND 5 FEET BEYOND THE LIMITS OF TRENCHING OR AS ORDERED BY THE ENGINEER.' and '2. ALL JOINTS TO BE SEALED WITH ASPHALT EMULSION (AC-20)'. The bottom right corner is marked 'NO SCALE'.</figure>\n\n[⚜️]\nALBANY\nNEW YORK | EST. 1686\n[⚜️]\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer\n\n\n<table>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY - DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br>PAVEMENT MILLING AND<br>STREET RESTORATION<br>(REQUIRED LIMITS OF WORK ARE CURB TO CURB)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No.<br>SR-3</td><td>FILE NAME:<br>SR-3.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED<br>05/01/02</td><td>REVISION DATE<br>03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">\n\n<description>This is a technical cross-section diagram illustrating a pavement repair or construction detail. The diagram displays a horizontal surface of pavers with specific structural layers beneath a central section.</description> \n\n1. **Top Surface**: A continuous row of pavers is shown. The section directly above the excavation is labeled \"18\" MIN\" on both sides, indicating \"LIMITS OF DISTURBANCE\" for the repair area. The pavers outside this central zone are labeled \"EXISTING PAVERS (TYP)\". \n\n2. **Structural Layers (from top to bottom)**:\n- **Top Layer**: \"RESET PAVERS IN MORTAR SETTING BED, 6\"± TOTAL DEPTH, MORTAR PAVER JOINTS WITH NON SHRINK GROUT\".\n- **Middle Layer**: \"8\" CONCRETE FOUNDATION CLASS 'C' CONCRETE\" containing \"WIRE FABRIC FOR CONCRETE REINFORCEMENT, NYSDOT SPECIFICATION\".\n- **Bottom Layer**: \"12\" SUBBASE COURSE\".\n\n3. **Excavation Detail**: Below the subbase course, a dashed outline represents the \"EXCAVATION LIMITS\". Inside this area is the label \"TRENCH BACKFILL, BACKFILL IN 6\" LIFTS, COMPACT PER SPECIFICATIONS\".</figure>\n\nNOTE:\n1. HISTORIC DISTRICT LIMITS:\nMADISON AVENUE: LARK STREET TO THE HUDSON RIVER\nLARK STREET: MADISON AVENUE TO CLINTON AVENUE\nCLINTON AVENUE: LARK STREET TO HUDSON RIVER\n2. CONTRACTOR SHALL NOTIFY CITY ENGINEER'S OFFICE 72\nHOURS PRIOR TO COMMENCING RESTORATION FOR\nINSPECTION OF THE RESTORATION.\n3. ALL WORK SHALL BE COMPLETED TO THE SATISFACTION\nOF THE CITY.\nNO SCALE\n\n\n[⚜]\nALBANY\nNEW YORK | EST. 1686\n[⚜]\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer\n\n\n<table>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY - DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br>STREET RESTORATION – GRANITE/BRICK<br>PAVEMENT WITHIN HISTORIC DISTRICT<br>(EXPOSED COBBLES)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>DETAIL No.<br>SR-4</td><td>FILE NAME:<br>SR-4.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED<br>03/21/04</td><td>REVISION DATE<br>03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">\n\n<description>This diagram illustrates a cross-section detail of concrete pavement construction, highlighting key components and specifications.</description> The text at the top left specifies: \"6” FOR DRIVEWAYS AND TRAFFIC AREAS 4” FOR ALL OTHER AREAS,\" with a leader line pointing to the concrete thickness. The diagram shows two concrete panels separated by a joint. Above the joint, it is labeled: \"PREMOLDED BITUMINOUS EXPANSION JOINT FILLER W/ SEALANT AT 20' O.C.\" Below the panels, there is a layer of crushed stone, labeled: \"6” MIN. CRUSHED STONE, TYPE 2.\" The concrete panels themselves contain a reinforcement layer, indicated by a leader line pointing to the interior of the concrete: \"6”x6”xW4xW4 REINFORCING MESH AT MID DEPTH.\" The horizontal distance between the start of the panels and the joint is marked as \"PANEL LAYOUT AOBE\".</figure>\n\n<table>\n<tr><td colspan=\"3\">DESIGN ELEMENT TOLERANCES</td></tr>\n<tr><td>ELEMENT</td><td>DESIGN AND FIELD LAYOUT LIMIT</td><td>LIMIT FOR WORK ACCEPTANCE</td></tr>\n<tr><td>SIDEWALK CROSS SLOPE</td><td>1.5% MAX.</td><td>2.0% MAX.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>SIDEWALK GRADE (RUNNING SLOPE)</td><td>4.5% MAX.</td><td>5.0% MAX.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>CURB RAMP GRADE (RUNNING SLOPE)</td><td>7.5% MAX.</td><td>8.3% MAX.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>BLENDED TRANSITION GRADE (RUNNING SLOPE)</td><td>4.5% MAX.</td><td>5.0% MAX.</td></tr>\n</table>\n\nNOTE: REFER TO NYSDOT STANDARD SHEETS 608-01.\n\nNOTES:\n1. THE CONCRETE USED SHALL BE PORTLAND CEMENT, AIR-ENTRAINED,\nCLASS \"A\" CONCRETE WITH AN AIR CONTENT OF 5%, MIN., TO 7%, MAX.,\nAND A SLUMP OF THREE INCHES, MIN., TO FIVE INCHES, MAX. NO FLY ASH\nAND MIN. 4,000 PSI.\n2. ALL SIDEWALKS SHALL BE FINISHED WITH A BROOM FINISH UNLESS\nDIRECTED OTHERWISE BY THE CITY.\n3. EXPANSION JOINTS TO BE PLACED BETWEEN ADJACENT SLABS, AT\nBUILDING LINE, AT CURBS, OR AT PENETRATING STRUCTURES.\n4. SIDEWALKS SHALL BE INSTALLED WITH A MAXIMUM CROSS SLOPE OF 2.0%\n5. ALL SIDEWALKS PANEL REPLACEMENT SHALL BE UP TO THE NEAREST\nSIDEWALK JOINT. NO PARTIAL PANEL REPLACEMENT IS ALLOWED\nNO SCALE\n\n\n<table>\n<tr><td rowspan=\"2\">⚜️<br>ALBANY<br>NEW YORK | EST. 1686<br>⚜️</td><td colspan=\"4\">CITY OF ALBANY - DEPARTMENT OF ENGINEERING</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"4\">DETAIL NAME:<br>SIDEWALK INSTALLATION<br>DETAIL</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Katherine M. Sheehan, Mayor<br>Howard M. Goebel P.E., City Engineer</td><td>DETAIL No.<br>SW-1</td><td>FILE NAME:<br>SW-1.DWG</td><td>DATE ISSUED<br>05/01/02</td><td>REVISION DATE<br>03/08/24</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<!-- PAGE BREAK -->\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">\n\n<description>This diagram illustrates the technical specifications for a pedestrian crosswalk design, specifically showing the layout of a zebra-style crossing connecting to a curb ramp.</description>\n\n### Transcription of labels and dimensions:\n- **CURB LINE**: Points to the curved edge of the sidewalk/curb.\n- **RAMP**: Points to the concrete, textured ramp area connecting the street to the curb.\n- **WHITE EPOXY REFLECTORIZED PAVEMENT STRIPES**: Points to the individual rectangular crosswalk stripes.\n- **8' MIN. PER CITY OF ALBANY TRAFFIC ENGINEERING**: Specifies the minimum width of the crosswalk.\n- **6\"**: Indicates the width of the gap or margin on the outer edges of the stripes.\n- **12\"**: Indicates the width of the individual white stripes.\n- **36\"**: Indicates the spacing between the white stripes.\n- **NOTE:**: A heading at the bottom left, though the content is not provided.</figure>\n\nNOTE:\n1. EPOXY TO COMPLY WITH NYSDOT STANDARDS\n2. MUTCD MANUAL, SECTION 3B SHALL BE USED PER CITY OF ALBANY\nTRAFFIC ENGINEERING RECOMMENDATIONS.\nNO SCALE\n\n\n⚜\nALBANY\nNEW YORK | EST. 1686\n⚜\nKatherine M. Sheehan, Mayor\nHoward M. Goebel P.E., 